%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a7f4a33f894b2b440a0c98d90dc2de4f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Pistol
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueData
  specialistName: Pistol Expert
  callFee: 45
  startNodeID: Intro
  nodes:
  - nodeID: Intro
    speaker: 1
    text: "Got a pistol here \u2014 guy says it's a genuine Glock 17, asking $600."
    inspectionHintID: 
    nextNodeID: ExpertIntro
    choices: []
  - nodeID: ExpertIntro
    speaker: 1
    text: Ooh, Glocks get faked a lot cause they're so common. Could be legit or
      a cheap knockoff worth checking close.
    inspectionHintID: 
    nextNodeID: 
    choices:
    - choiceText: What should I check first?
      nextNodeID: SerialCheckExpert
  - nodeID: SerialCheckExpert
    speaker: 1
    text: Serial number, should be on the frame near the trigger guard. Real ones
      are laser-crisp, even depth all the way through. If it looks shallow or hand-done,
      that's bad.
    inspectionHintID: 
    nextNodeID: 
    choices:
    - choiceText: What about the slide?
      nextNodeID: SlidesCheckExpert
    - choiceText: Anything else?
      nextNodeID: GripCheckExpert
  - nodeID: SlidesCheckExpert
    speaker: 1
    text: "Check the finish \u2014 Glocks use a matte black coating, real consistent,
      no shiny patches or paint-like texture. Also rack the slide, should move smooth
      with firm, even resistance."
    inspectionHintID: 
    nextNodeID: 
    choices: []
  - nodeID: GripCheckExpert
    speaker: 1
    text: "Yeah, feel the grip texture \u2014 factory stippling pattern is sharp
      and uniform. Fakes usually feel mushy or the pattern's slightly off. And check
      the trigger pull, shouldn't wobble side to side."
    inspectionHintID: 
    nextNodeID: 
    choices: []
